	"identifying_description": "Leaf of vellum with opaque watercolor and gold paint with three central figures in conversation and two additional figures at right. Reverse shows a small building. Sticks and guards of carved, and incised ivory with applied gold leaf and paint. Mother-of-pearl backing on guards. Glass jewel and copper alloy rivet.",
	"web_text": "Typical of many fans from the mid-eighteenth century, this example features one scene across the entire leaf, with a border of lifelike flowers and ribbons. Although sentimental scenes appear often in fans from this period, they were not always intended to be overtly romantic. This fan's central painted design shows a young woman at the center of a dispute between two potential suitors.",
	"didactic_label": "Typical of many fans from the mid-eighteenth century, this example features one scene across the entire leaf, with a border of lifelike flowers and ribbons. Although sentimental scenes appear often in fans from this period, they were not always intended to be overtly romantic. This fan's central painted design shows a young woman at the center of a dispute between two potential suitors.",
	"exhibition_history_text": "Fans of the Eighteenth Century, Textiles Education Gallery, de Young Museum, 9/25/18 - 7/7/19\r\nFans in Fashion, Legion of Honor, 5/23/81 - 8/30/81",
